-- Passage wg12-paragraph-transitions-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('e683a37d-9d9f-5316-b63f-451ab50b0507', 'wg12-paragraph-transitions-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-paragraph-transitions'), null,
        '9-12', $q$A Bus Schedule Built by Students$q$, $q$(1) Last year, our town's youth advisory council took on a question that affected hundreds of students: why did so few teenagers ride the public bus? (2) The council began by surveying more than four hundred students at the two high schools. (3) The responses pointed to a clear pattern. (4) Most students did not describe the buses as unsafe or uncomfortable; ____, they said the buses simply did not run at the times students needed them, especially after practices and club meetings ended.

(5) Armed with these results, the council met with the transit planners. (6) The planners explained that adding late buses would cost money the agency did not have. (7) ____, they agreed to study whether shifting existing trips later in the afternoon would serve more riders without adding expense. (8) Council members helped by counting riders at three stops over two weeks. (9) The council also organized a car wash to raise money for the school library's book fair.

(10) The trial schedule began in January, with the last two afternoon buses leaving forty minutes later than before. (11) Within two months, afternoon ridership among students had nearly doubled, and adult riders who worked late shifts benefited from the later trips as well.$q$, 'draft')
