  ('e35493d9-ad0e-5964-a841-674fa6182ee5', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'medium',
   $q$A paragraph explains that online visitors can zoom in on brushstrokes too small to see in a gallery, that researchers abroad can study objects without traveling, and that fragile items too delicate to display can still be viewed. Which topic sentence best introduces the paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Digitizing a museum's collection opens it to audiences and uses that a gallery alone cannot serve.","is_correct":true},{"text":"High-resolution cameras can capture brushstrokes in remarkable detail when the lighting is right.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Museums have collected and displayed valuable objects for many centuries in many countries.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-broad"},{"text":"Many museums charge admission fees to help pay for guards, lighting, and repairs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Digitizing a museum's collection opens it to audiences and uses that a gallery alone cannot serve.$q$, $q$All three details describe new audiences or uses made possible by digital collections, and the correct choice names that shared idea. The sentence about cameras and brushstrokes fits only the first detail, so it is too narrow to introduce the whole paragraph.$q$, 'draft', null)
