  ('9dc8ff90-53a2-5631-9888-9199d69f2f40', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Read: "(1) Three years ago, the town restored a drained wetland on the edge of the river. (2) During heavy rains, the wetland now absorbs water that once flooded nearby streets. (3) It also filters runoff before that water reaches the river. (4) Wetlands in many regions were drained centuries ago to create farmland. (5) Birdwatchers have reported several species returning to the area for the first time in decades." Which sentence should be removed because it does not support the paragraph's main idea?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Sentence 4","is_correct":true},{"text":"Sentence 3","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-supporting-detail"},{"text":"Sentence 5","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misjudges-relevant-benefit"},{"text":"Sentence 1","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-topic-sentence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Sentence 4$q$, $q$Sentences 2, 3, and 5 each describe a benefit the town has gained from its restored wetland, while sentence 4 is general history about other places. Sentence 5 may seem different because it concerns birds rather than water, but returning wildlife is still a benefit of the restoration.$q$, 'draft', null)
