  ('597e0ce4-0b29-5fa0-81a2-ae1362031f8b', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'medium',
   $q$One paragraph ends: "For decades, weather forecasters relied on reports sent by telegraph from distant observation stations." Which sentence best opens the next paragraph, which describes how satellites changed forecasting?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Satellites orbit the planet at different heights depending on the jobs they are designed to do.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-previous-paragraph"},{"text":"Weather forecasts are now available on phones, televisions, and radios throughout the day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"skips-logical-step"},{"text":"Those reports covered only the stations themselves, but satellites later showed entire storm systems at once.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Telegraph operators had to learn a code of short and long signals to send each message.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-next-paragraph"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Those reports covered only the stations themselves, but satellites later showed entire storm systems at once.$q$, $q$The correct sentence points back to the telegraph reports and names their limit, then introduces satellites as the improvement, so it links both paragraphs. The sentence about satellite orbits introduces the new topic but drops the connection to the telegraph reports.$q$, 'draft', null)
