  ('f91ca180-a441-526e-9a05-c8ee5f6cac18', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read: "(1) Orienteering races test navigation as much as fitness. (2) Runners receive a map at the start line and must find a series of checkpoints in order. (3) ____ (4) A fast runner who misreads the map can easily lose to a slower one who plans carefully." Which sentence best fills blank 3?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The checkpoints are usually marked with orange and white flags that hang from posts or trees.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Orienteering began as a training exercise and later became a popular sport in many countries.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"},{"text":"Because the route between checkpoints is not marked, each runner must decide which path to take.","is_correct":true},{"text":"For this reason, the fastest runners nearly always win the race by a wide margin.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-following-sentence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because the route between checkpoints is not marked, each runner must decide which path to take.$q$, $q$The correct sentence explains why navigation matters, which sets up sentence 4's point that a careful planner can beat a faster runner. The sentence claiming the fastest runners nearly always win contradicts sentence 4.$q$, 'draft', null)
