  ('1c72800b-5f5c-5354-9b2f-c1fe76423bc2', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Read: "(1) The city should build protected bike lanes on Harbor Avenue. (2) Collisions between cars and cyclists on the avenue have risen in each of the past three years. (3) Protected lanes separate the two with raised curbs, which makes such collisions far less likely. (4) Yet studies of similar streets suggest that customers who arrive by bike tend to visit shops more often. (5) A safer, busier avenue would benefit everyone who uses it." Where should this sentence be added: "Some shop owners worry that losing parking spaces will drive customers away"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"After sentence 5","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"concern-after-conclusion"},{"text":"After sentence 1","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"concern-before-claim-support"},{"text":"After sentence 4","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"concern-after-rebuttal"},{"text":"After sentence 3","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$After sentence 3$q$, $q$Sentence 4 begins with "Yet" and answers a worry about customers, so the shop owners' concern must come right before it, after sentence 3. Placing it after sentence 4 would put the objection after the reply, leaving "Yet" with nothing to answer.$q$, 'draft', null)
